4... Bg4
{ Black immediately pins the knight with bishop g4. This is the case where you counterpin with Bb5 if you haven't moved your bishop yet. Key recommendation: if they pin your knight early before you've moved your bishop, counterpin their knight. }
5. Bb5
{ Counterpin! Bishop to b5 - the key recommendation when they pin your knight early. We don't want a knight jumping to d4 and causing problems. The reason is simple: we don't want to deal with a knight coming in and attacking our pinned knight. }
5... a6 { Black pushes a6 to challenge the bishop. } 6. Bxc6+
{ White trades bishop for knight, eliminating the threat of a knight jumping to d4. }
6... bxc6 7. O-O { White castles. After castling, chase the bishop away. } 7...
